<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετανάστ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταναστῆναι</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερανάστης</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one
				who has left his home, wanderer, migrant</i>, commonly as a
			term of reproach, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτίμητος μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.648
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῦνοι οὐ μετανάσται
			Ἑλλήνων</span>, of the Athenians, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.161
			</span></i>; <i>fugitive,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				487.18
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				439
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. γενόμενοι ὑπὸ
				ἐθνῶν</span> Prisc.<i><span class="en">
				p.341
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετανίσταντο</span> ibid.):
			c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετῆς μ.</span>
			<i>from</i> virtue, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.415
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				477
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάτρης μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					2.420
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
			<i>wandering</i>, of <i>the planets</i>, opp. the fixed stars,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				457
			</span></i>:—hence fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταναστ-νάστις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ σώματος
				μ.</span> a <i>fugitive</i> from . . , <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.462
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταναστ-νάστρια</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπέλων μ. πέρδιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.204
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>).</div>
